# Modem and digital-voice roadmap — October 2026
#
# Persistent document: see doc/dsp-workers.md for architecture and progress.
#
# Goal: enable hardware developers to bring up new RF waveforms without
# writing new rrserver, rrclient or GUI code. DSP implementations are
# isolated external executables, never loaded into rrserver.
#
# Priorities BEFORE SDR work (tentatively January 2027):
# [ ] Build/test existing rig RX PCM -> modem FD 4 path, including partial writes,
#     frame boundaries, sample rate and queue overflow diagnostics.
# [ ] Replace raw PCM assumptions with source-declared format negotiation,
#     bounded nonblocking frame queues and timestamps/discontinuity flags.
# [ ] Implement worker control socket: hello, config, heartbeat, PTT leases,
#     frequency/mode/VFO queries and updates via the existing rig backend.
# [ ] Ensure PTT-off on crash, EOF, watchdog, lost authorization and restart.
# [ ] Restrict TX PCM injection to explicitly admitted/authorized workers.
# [ ] Bind worker lifecycle/configuration to a rig, not to a terminal.
# [ ] Expose resources, worker health, codec settings and permissions in
#     Resource Explorer and serial clients. Keep ttyCAT/GPS/MODEM floating PTYs.
# [ ] Add RX-only sample decoder worker and tests that operate unattended,
#     without a connected terminal or client subscriber.
# [ ] Add modem log rotation/replay tests, session correlation (non-secret ID),
#     and loss/discontinuity events. See per-modem log example in rrserver.cfg.
# [ ] Make shipped examples and actual default configs agree on documented
#     supported keys. Unimplemented examples MUST stay commented.
#
# Long-term WISHLIST (not implementation claims):
# [ ] Persistent decoder-only workers per VFO and named RX audio source; multiple
#     independent decoders can subscribe to the same stream.
# [ ] Source abstraction: rig RX, VFO RX, saved recording, SDR channelizer
#     slice / virtual receiver, or generated test signal.
# [ ] Canonical immutable slice names include source, RF center Hz, bandwidth Hz,\n#     sample rate, sample format/layout and processing versions, so multiple\n#     decoders share a single slice. Keep VFO aliases mutable and distinct.\n# [ ] Source metadata: parent rig, RF center frequency, offset, bandwidth,
#     sample rate/format, VFO, timestamps and discontinuity indications.
# [ ] Auto-start configured receivers when a compatible source becomes
#     available, and reattach safely when it disappears/reappears.
# [ ] SDR support (target January 2027): channelize wideband IQ into
#     narrowband per-frequency PCM slices and run independent decoders.
# [ ] Potential FT8 monitors across multiple frequencies/bands IF front-end
#     instantaneous bandwidth and RF hardware support simultaneous coverage.
#     Multi-band coverage may require multiple receivers or scheduled tuning.
# [ ] Worker scheduler/cost controls (CPU, memory, decoder count, prioritization),
#     stream observability, and remote results without shipping raw IQ.
# [ ] Standalone third-party codecs: PSK31, RTTY, packet, ARDOP-like,
#     JS8-compatible adapters, FreeDV/digital voice (PCM speech <-> RF PCM).
# [ ] Operator sets starting VFO/frequency; individual workers may optionally
#     receive temporary, independently revocable tuning/PTT privileges.
# [ ] Generic parameter schema -> settings UI; development-friendly worker SDK
#     and sample programs, independent of GStreamer/GTK and language choice.
#
# Always preserve: readable C, three-space indentation, fault isolation,
# bounded queues, clear compatibility guarantees, and server-side auth.
